module Math3D

# Each declaration below creates nothing: `@rf` names the shared declaration it shows, and validate-stdlib
# checks that the two still match.

### Represents the crashable raised by `inverse()` and `solve(b:)` of `Matrix2R2C`, `Matrix3R3C` and
### `Matrix4R4C` when the matrix is singular: Gaussian elimination with partial pivoting met a pivot that is
### exactly 0. A matrix that is only close to singular has an inverse, and its result can be inaccurate.
@rf("SingularMatrixError")
crashable SingularMatrixError
    ### Stores the number of rows (and columns) of the matrix.
    size: U64

### Returns the message naming the size of the singular matrix.
### :returns: The resulting `Text` value.
@rf("SingularMatrixError.crash_message")
routine SingularMatrixError.crash_message() -> Text
